{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_70223d0a", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:26:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to kick off a discussion about our new feature for customizable dashboards. I've found some similar features in open-source projects that might give us some insights. Let's dive in! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260924-0-97fc5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-0-97fc5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_70223d0a", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:30:00", "text": "First up, Grafana has a feature called Role-Based Dashboard Customization. It allows users to customize dashboards based on their roles, which seems pretty aligned with what we're aiming for. Here's the link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/4921. What do you guys think? @eid_13df35ed", "utterranceID": "20260924-1-305cb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-1-305cb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13df35ed", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:34:00", "text": "Thanks, David! Grafana's approach sounds quite similar to ours. I like how they focus on role-based customization, which could help us ensure that users see only what's relevant to them. We should definitely consider how they handle permissions and user roles. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260924-2-76431"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-2-76431"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_76d9cb07", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:39:00", "text": "Agreed, George. Grafana's implementation might give us some good ideas on managing user roles effectively. We should also look at how they handle the UI for customization. It could be a great reference point.", "utterranceID": "20260924-3-204d5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-3-204d5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_70223d0a", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:42:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at Kibana's User-Specific Visualization Panels. This feature allows users to create and save visualization panels tailored to their roles and data analysis needs. Check it out here: https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/4922. Thoughts? @eid_76d9cb07", "utterranceID": "20260924-4-0dcb3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-4-0dcb3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_76d9cb07", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:45:00", "text": "Kibana's feature is interesting because it emphasizes user-specific panels. This could be useful for us to consider how we allow users to save and manage their customizations. It might be worth exploring how they handle data persistence and user preferences. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260924-5-55f6f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-5-55f6f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-cf7cd7"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13df35ed", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T17:48:00", "text": "I agree, David. Kibana's focus on user-specific needs could help us refine our approach to personalization. We should also think about how we can make it easy for users to switch between different saved configurations.", "utterranceID": "20260924-6-42a4d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260924-6-42a4d"}

