{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidtaylor-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-e2bea9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1bf91687", "timestamp": "2026-06-23T18:23:00", "text": "Kubernetes is always a good reference. Their API server is a critical component, so their OAuth 2.0 implementation must be solid. We should see how they manage user roles and permissions with OAuth. Could be beneficial for us. 🔐", "utterranceID": "20260623-5-eea03"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260623-5-eea03"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidtaylor-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-e2bea9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edc07895", "timestamp": "2026-06-23T18:28:00", "text": "Absolutely, Julia! Kubernetes' approach to roles and permissions could definitely inform our strategy. Lastly, let's check out Grafana's PR. They've added OAuth 2.0 for securing data source plugins: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/2358. Any thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260623-6-5cb84"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260623-6-5cb84"}
